{"id":"shinjuku","name":"Shinjuku","qid":"Q179645","country":"Japan","locality":"Tokyo","lat":"35.693888888","lon":"139.703416666","built":"1947","year":1947,"year_text":"1947","century":"20th century","era":"20th century and later","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"","heritage":"","type":"special ward of Japan","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinjuku","text":"Shinjuku (新宿区, Shinjuku-ku) [ɕìɲ̟́.ɟ̟͡ʑɨ́.kɯ̈́, -kɯ̥̈.kɯ̈̀, ɕíɲ̟́-] , officially called Shinjuku City, is one of the 23 special wards of Tokyo. Since the end of World War II, Shinjuku has become a major secondary center of Tokyo (fukutoshin), rivaling the original city center in Marunouchi. Today, it is a major commercial and administrative center and houses the northern half of Shinjuku Station, the busiest railway station in the world, as well as the Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building, the administrative center of the Tokyo Metropolitan Government.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shinjuku","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[],"depictions":[{"id":"persona-5--shinjuku","game":"persona-5","name":"Shinjuku","verified":false,"text":"Shinjuku (新宿) is a location in the series.","text_source":"https://megamitensei.fandom.com/wiki/Shinjuku","text_license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","images":[{"id":"gh-69012dcdb784","w":1024,"h":768,"credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Persona 5, © ; Deep Silver.","source":"https://megamitensei.fandom.com/wiki/File:Shinjuku_Field.jpg","via":"Fandom (megamitensei)","note":"Fandom upload by Zettaizetsubou on 2014-02-19"}},{"id":"gh-69cfd494a343","w":980,"h":700,"credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Persona 5, © ; Deep Silver.","source":"https://megamitensei.fandom.com/wiki/File:Shin_Megami_Tensei_Akira_Kenai_shinjuku.png","via":"Fandom (megamitensei)","note":"Fandom upload by 17IdkNamesAreHard171 on 2020-12-15"}},{"id":"gh-ba128f7a1e44","w":512,"h":512,"credit":{"text":"Screenshot from Persona 5, © ; Deep Silver.","source":"https://megamitensei.fandom